WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.325 --> 00:00:05.560
Savannah is in Charlotte

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:06.265
Hi Savannah how are you?

00:00:06.265 --> 00:00:08.025
I'm good how are you, Dave?

00:00:08.025 --> 00:00:09.285
 

00:00:09.285 --> 00:00:11.115
Better than I deserve, what's up?

00:00:11.605 --> 00:00:14.505
All right. So I'm 22 and

00:00:14.505 --> 00:00:17.420
I'm about to start my first job out of college

00:00:17.555 --> 00:00:20.465
The company is there's a lot of travel involved with the job

00:00:20.465 --> 00:00:23.445
And the company

00:00:23.445 --> 00:00:26.555
requires that I pay out of pocket

00:00:26.555 --> 00:00:29.515
and then they reimburse me and they suggest I get a credit card

00:00:29.515 --> 00:00:32.845
to pay those expenses first, but I don't want to do that.

00:00:32.845 --> 00:00:34.885
So how should I work around that?

00:00:35.245 --> 00:00:37.345
Um, do you have any money?

00:00:37.865 --> 00:00:40.925
Yeah I do. I'm going into Baby Step 4.

00:00:40.925 --> 00:00:43.955
Good. Good for you. Well done.

00:00:44.225 --> 00:00:47.405
Well, um, how big of a company is it?

00:00:48.125 --> 00:00:50.915
Um, it's a medium-sized

00:00:50.915 --> 00:00:53.785
company. 250 employees

00:00:53.785 --> 00:00:56.785
OK.

00:00:56.785 --> 00:00:59.660
Well why don't you talk to someone in leadership

00:00:59.845 --> 00:01:02.715
and explain to them that you don't borrow money

00:01:02.865 --> 00:01:04.200
and I don't use credit cards

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:04.955
 

00:01:04.955 --> 00:01:06.485
so I won't be getting a credit card

00:01:07.055 --> 00:01:09.835
I really don't think it's right that

00:01:09.835 --> 00:01:13.205
I'm using my money to travel for your company

00:01:13.535 --> 00:01:16.015
And so um I'd like for you all to furnish me a

00:01:16.015 --> 00:01:19.265
card. I don't think that'll work.

00:01:19.265 --> 00:01:21.845
I want you to try it with humility

00:01:21.845 --> 00:01:24.455
and kindness, not being a jerk about it

00:01:24.455 --> 00:01:26.155
I'm not suggesting you do something to lose your job

00:01:26.705 --> 00:01:29.405
or that you have an attitude or something

00:01:29.405 --> 00:01:32.185
And just go, "Hey, I'm 22

00:01:32.185 --> 00:01:35.005
"I just got out of college. I am not

00:01:35.045 --> 00:01:37.875
"borrowing money. I'm not gonna get into debt.

00:01:38.275 --> 00:01:40.325
"And so you guys gotta help me, OK?

00:01:40.325 --> 00:01:43.465
"Cause I'm not taking out a credit card.

00:01:43.465 --> 00:01:45.925
"Is there any way you could just furnish me a card?"

00:01:45.925 --> 00:01:48.265
"Cause by the way, all this stuff I'm doing I'm doing for you."

00:01:48.315 --> 00:01:51.815
"I'm not gonna put anything on the card that isn't company."

00:01:51.985 --> 00:01:54.175
"And if I do you can fire me."

00:01:54.215 --> 00:01:57.345
I don't think they'll do it. But I would ask. OK?

00:01:57.345 --> 00:01:58.925
If that doesn't work,

00:01:59.705 --> 00:02:02.725
then what we suggest to people is,

00:02:02.725 --> 00:02:05.495
two other options. One is, get a different job.

00:02:05.495 --> 00:02:07.805
Which is unreasonable, probably.

00:02:07.805 --> 00:02:10.385
The second option is for you to get a

00:02:10.385 --> 00:02:12.385
separate checking account just for travel.

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:15.685
Put a debit card on it and put

00:02:15.685 --> 00:02:16.875
the amount in there that you need

00:02:16.875 --> 00:02:19.445
for monthly travel expenses

00:02:19.445 --> 00:02:22.805
And you only have to "prime the pump" so to speak one time

00:02:23.135 --> 00:02:25.935
And so, you estimate

00:02:25.935 --> 00:02:27.905
what your monthly travel is going to be--Do you have any idea what that's going to be

00:02:28.425 --> 00:02:31.105
Um, well to start out, I'll be doing a lot of training

00:02:31.105 --> 00:02:34.085
so I won't be traveling consistently for about six months

00:02:34.085 --> 00:02:36.945
so I don't know what the monthly expenses will be

00:02:36.945 --> 00:02:39.635
OK. Won't be much then.

00:02:39.635 --> 00:02:42.585
But let's just use

00:02:42.585 --> 00:02:43.585
Is it monthly that they reimburse?

00:02:44.155 --> 00:02:47.275
Um, it's every pay check. Every two weeks

00:02:47.275 --> 00:02:50.345
OK. All right. So really all we have to worry about is two week's worth of travel.

00:02:50.595 --> 00:02:53.505
So let's pretend two weeks worth of travel was $1,000.

00:02:53.505 --> 00:02:56.175
OK?

00:02:56.175 --> 00:02:58.545
If you put $1000 in this checking account or

00:02:58.545 --> 00:02:59.965
$1200 in the checking account

00:03:00.615 --> 00:03:02.485
And you use your debit card.

00:03:02.485 --> 00:03:05.765
And you use your money. You turn it in

00:03:06.055 --> 00:03:08.855
They give you a check for $1000.

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:10.855
You put the $1000 back in this account

00:03:11.655 --> 00:03:15.005
You see what I'm saying? You only have to put it in there one time. And you're using

00:03:15.005 --> 00:03:18.145
your money but

00:03:18.145 --> 00:03:20.995
they're reimbursing you which is what you're doing by the way

00:03:20.995 --> 00:03:21.995
when you use a credit card.

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:24.040
-Yeah.
-I mean, what if they didn't pay you?

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:24.805
 

00:03:25.125 --> 00:03:27.495
Well, you'd have credit card debt.

00:03:27.495 --> 00:03:30.605
Well, you've lost the money.

00:03:30.605 --> 00:03:33.805
Guess what? You've lost the money either way. That' s the weird thing

00:03:33.805 --> 00:03:35.845
So I don't have anybody

00:03:35.845 --> 00:03:38.595
on my team that I ask

00:03:38.595 --> 00:03:40.495
to travel with their personal money.

00:03:41.475 --> 00:03:43.400
-OK
-We always furnish the money

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:44.185
for them to travel

00:03:44.185 --> 00:03:47.125
Either furnish them a debit card from our company

00:03:47.125 --> 00:03:49.415
if they travel a lot. Or,

00:03:49.415 --> 00:03:52.795
We advance them petty cash to pay for the travel

00:03:52.795 --> 00:03:55.275
and we pay for the expenses. And they can't turn in anything

00:03:55.275 --> 00:03:58.155
on that debit card obviously

00:03:58.155 --> 00:04:00.545
or on that petty cash receipt that isn't

00:04:00.545 --> 00:04:03.465
you know, I'm not buying their shampoo, OK? I'm not

00:04:03.465 --> 00:04:06.095
buying a dress for you while you're on the road. That's your problem.

00:04:06.095 --> 00:04:08.525
I'm talking about usable company expenses

00:04:08.525 --> 00:04:09.895
for travel.

00:04:10.615 --> 00:04:13.875
And uh, that's what you limit it to.

00:04:13.875 --> 00:04:17.205
Be very, very careful that you don't use it for anything that isn't reimbursable

00:04:17.235 --> 00:04:19.785
And then the money will always go right back to the account.

00:04:20.105 --> 00:04:23.005
And the only thing you're at risk is two weeks

00:04:23.005 --> 00:04:24.005
worth of travel.

00:04:24.405 --> 00:04:27.235
And that works really well for people who travel a lot.

00:04:27.675 --> 00:04:30.755
And the debit card by the way on the road will do everything

00:04:30.755 --> 00:04:31.845
your credit card will do.

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:34.665
I've heard people say "Well it doesn't work

00:04:34.665 --> 00:04:37.225
"internationally." Well I just returned from 3 weeks in Europe. I just got back.

00:04:37.645 --> 00:04:40.245
I didn't have one single episode

00:04:40.245 --> 00:04:43.265
Not one negative episode with my debit card.

00:04:43.385 --> 00:04:46.155
Not one. Everyone took it.

00:04:46.155 --> 00:04:49.125
Just like a credit card. Guess what? That's basically what it is.

00:04:49.125 --> 00:04:51.435
Except it's using the money out of your account.

00:04:51.845 --> 00:04:54.935
Hey guys thanks for watching! If you enjoyed this

00:04:54.985 --> 00:04:57.905
video, click the subscribe button!

